-- title:
--   Product of component ideal sheaves on Y equals (q)
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\neq 0$ and a prime $q$ with $q\nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel.html#L71). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain equipped with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O$ from $R=\mathbb{Z}$ localised at $q$ (the subring [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.R q`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel.html#L32) of $\mathbb{Q}$), and assume the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by the image of $q$, so $q$ is a uniformiser. Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $t\colon O\to\kappa$ a ring homomorphism, and assume the node type [`V3Glue.LevelSite.Node 𝔛 κ (t ∘ ρO)`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel.html#L42) — the fibre product of the two component maps $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}$ over $\kappa$ — is finite. Let $H$ be the package [`V3AsmLevel.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel.html#L270) of site hypotheses (finiteness of the nodes, existence of oriented crossing charts, an étale neighbourhood datum, injectivity and closedness of the crossing points, and the model hypotheses on $q$ and $O$), and suppose each of the two marked points $\xi_j$, $j\in\{0,1\}$, lies in the open set `X0` of the chart input $C$, that is, in the complement of the finitely many marked points of the charts. Then for every affine open $U$ of the glued scheme $Y=$ [`V3AsmLevel.Y`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel.html#L288), the ideal at $U$ of the product over all $v$ in the component index type `X0MqComponents (width …)` of the ideal sheaf data [`V3AsmLevel.comp … v`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel.html#L410) equals the ideal of $\Gamma(Y,U)$ generated by the image of $q$.
--
--   This records that the scheme-theoretic sum of the components of the special fibre of the glued resolution $Y$ — the strict transforms of the two branches together with the exceptional lines over the crossings, each with multiplicity one — is exactly the divisor cut out by the uniformiser $q$, so that the special fibre of $Y\to\operatorname{Spec}O$ is reduced. It supplies the corresponding field in the construction of the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model package and its ramified charts, [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam).
